  "task_id": "five_agent_pipe_leak_repair",
  "instruction": "Detect and repair a seeded leak in the laboratory pipe rig with five coordinated robot controllers. B2 must carry the stowed Z1 thermal-camera arm to the pipe inspection viewpoint. Z1 must deploy, detect and localize the leak from measured thermal evidence, then stow before B2 moves. In parallel, the static Franka Panda must collect the single repair tool and place it in the shared handoff tray. The Franka mounted on Husky must load and secure that tool before Husky moves. After Z1 localizes the leak, Husky must drive to the leak-repair dock with its arm stowed; its mounted Franka must use the supplied tool to close the measured repair collar and return the tool to the Husky rack. Z1 must then verify from a second thermal observation that the leak is repaired. Every shared zone and route must be acquired and released explicitly, no robot may wait while holding a resource, all waits and acquisitions must be bounded, and both mobile platforms and all arms must finish home or stowed.",
